2. NOT IN operator:
It is a type of special operator which is similar to IN operator but instec of selecting the values it is used to reject the values present at RHS side of the condition.

--> To reject the multiple values from same column we use NOT IN operator.

syntax:
Column_Name NOT IN (val1, val2,.....valN)

---waqtd name, job, salary and hiredate of an employee except Miller, Turnerand KING

select ename,job, sal, hiredate
from emp
where ename not in ('MILLER', 'TURNER', 'KING');

3. BETWEEN operator:
It is a type of special operator which is used whenever we have a range of values.

BETWEEN operator always works including the range of values.

--->In the syntax of between we should never interchange the range of values

---> In BETWEEN operator we should enclose the ranges within the parenthesis.

syntax:
Column_Name between lower_range and higher_range

--> according to the question if the question has words like greater than, less than, more than, between, before and after words then in that case increase lower range by 1 and decrement the higher range by 1.

---waqtd name and salary of an employees who earns the salary more than 1250 and less than 3000

select ename,sal

from emp

where sal between 1251 and 2999;

---waqtd name,job and salary of an employees who are earning salary ranging from 1100 to 2950

select ENAME, JOB, SAL
from emp
where sal between 1100 and 2950;

4.NOT BETWEEN operator:

It is a type of special operator similar to BETWEEN operator but instead of selecting the values it is used to reject the range of values.

syntax:
Column_Name not between lower_range and higher-range

----waqtd name job hiredate and salary of an employees except those employees who earn the salary between 1500 to 3000

select ename,job, hiredate, sal
from emp
where sal not between 1501 and 2999;

5.IS Operator:

It is a type of special operator which is used to compare with theNULL's.

--->If the value is Null it. selects it if it is Not null it rejects.

---> Always IS operator must be used along with the NULL

syntax:
Column_Name IS NULL

---waqtd name, job, sal and comm of an employees who are earning no commission

select ename,job,sal,comm
from emp
where comm is null;

6. IS NOT:

It is a type of special operator similar to IS operator but instead of selecting the NULL it is used to reject the NULL.IS NOT operator must be used along with NULL keyword.

syntax:
Column Name IS NOT NULL:

---waqtd name job of an employees who are working in either of the job.

